HRIS: Employee, Leave & Payroll Management System
📌 Project Overview

This project is an Excel-based Human Resource Information System (HRIS) designed to manage essential HR operations in a structured and organized manner.

The system includes three main components:

👥 Employee Master
🗓️ Leave Tracker
💰 Payroll Tracker

It helps maintain employee information, monitor leave utilization, track Loss of Pay (LOP), and manage payroll-related information.

🎯 Project Objectives

The key objectives of this project are:

Maintain a centralized employee database.
Organize employee information efficiently.
Track employee leave utilization.
Monitor Casual and Sick Leave.
Identify unexcused absences.
Track Loss of Pay (LOP) days.
Support payroll-related HR operations.
Monitor basic employee and workforce metrics.
👥 Employee Master

The Employee Master sheet acts as the central database of the HRIS.

It contains the following employee details:

Field	Description
Emp ID	Unique identification number for each employee
Name	Employee name
Department	Employee's department
Designation	Employee's job role
Date of Joining	Date when the employee joined
Reporting Manager	Manager assigned to the employee
Salary Band	Employee salary category
Status	Active or Terminated
Performance Rating	Employee performance score
📊 Key Workforce Metrics

The Employee Master also tracks:

Total Headcount
Active Employees
Terminated Employees
Employee Turnover Rate
🗓️ Leave Tracker

The Leave Tracker helps monitor employee leave allocation and utilization.

It tracks:

Monthly Casual Leave Allowed
Monthly Sick Leave Allowed
Casual Leaves Taken
Sick Leaves Taken
Unexcused Absences
Total Leaves Taken
Casual Leave Balance
Sick Leave Balance
Loss of Pay (LOP) Days
Net Remaining Leave Balance
📌 Key Benefits

The Leave Tracker helps HR:

Monitor employee absenteeism.
Track leave utilization.
Identify employees with excessive leave.
Calculate remaining leave balances.
Identify Loss of Pay days.
💰 Payroll Tracker

The Payroll Tracker is designed to organize and monitor employee payroll-related information.

It supports HR operations by helping manage:

Employee salary information
Compensation details
Payroll-related records
Salary tracking
Payroll calculations
